{"chunk_id": "12351cde5123", "text": "After their wedding, Shiva and Parvati travel to Kailasa, the radiant Silver Mountain, where gods, spirits, and nature itself celebrate their arrival. The divine couple visit Rama\u2019s temple\u2014where witnesses mysteriously perceive them as Rama and Sita\u2014hinting at Shiva\u2019s cosmic play (lila). In Kailasa, their love unfolds in intimate, joyful scenes while Nandi guards their chamber. Meanwhile the demon Taraka terrorizes the gods. Vishnu explains that only a son of Shiva can defeat him and warns the gods not to disturb the divine couple. When they finally appeal, Shiva releases his seed through yogic power, angering Parvati, who longs for motherhood and curses the gods. The seed passes through Agni, Ganga, and the mountains until it manifests as the radiant six\u2011headed child Skanda (Kartikeya), destined to destroy Taraka and restore cosmic balance.\nAfter their wedding, Siva and Parvati dwell in love at Kailasa while the gods seek help against Taraka, leading to the miraculous birth of Skanda.\nThemes: divine marriage, cosmic duty vs desire, curse and divine intervention, miraculous birth, defeat of demon Taraka", "vector": [0.02138061821460724, -0.024510782212018967, -0.010265879333019257, 0.004857724066823721, -0.025823859497904778, 0.015809984877705574, -0.02859591320157051, -0.016605788841843605, -0.02562490850687027, -0.026155445724725723, 0.0008513451321050525, 0.019099310040473938, 0.006074641831219196, 0.0014349352568387985, 0.006333278492093086, 0.006349857896566391, 0.03177913278341293, -0.02441793866455555, 0.029895726591348648, -0.02051849663257599, -0.006217223592102528, 0.0031848764047026634, 0.0025764175225049257, -0.006449333392083645, -0.023887401446700096, 0.007845306769013405, 0.022149894386529922, -0.02387413941323757, 0.010000611655414104, -0.010464830324053764, -0.017680125311017036, -0.009456811472773552, -0.01274613756686449, -0.010564306750893593, -0.013939844444394112, -0.00567010790109